{"obsah":"<p><strong>A lookout tower record and two team exhibitions – Miskovice and Hořepník</strong><br><br>Sometimes ideas come up that turn out to be very much on the edge. One of them was the idea from Miskovice and Aleš Matoušek to try riding up the local 199-step lookout tower on a bike. The choice fell on Vlasta Kabeláč Čiháček, holder of the record for riding up and down the Petřín lookout tower.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>As it was an exhibition show, there was first a roughly 30-minute demonstration with egging on from Lukáš Valný and Tobík Dolák. Vlasta then took a few minutes' rest and set off to conquer the tower. Without any practice. The crisis came right after the first floor and only deepened. The steps were small for the larger diameter of mountain bike wheels, and the metal itself didn't help with grip either. In the end it took a third more hops than there were steps. From the second floor on: cramps and braking with two fingers. But the goal wasn't just to get to the top – which he did in 4:05 min – but also to get back down, and that's where the biggest problem arose. The Cube e-bike available was great, but the steps were small and had no barriers at the railings to prevent falls. Twice it already looked like a trip over the handlebars, arrow pointing down, because of the cramps in his hands, but luckily after two dabs Vlasta found his rhythm and rode down the floors partly on the front wheel, so he fitted safely. Down in 2:51 min, and an overall time of 6:56.74 min is beyond expectations given the preparation and conditions.<em> “After this I needed the whole day to pull myself together. I don't think I've ever been in worse physical shape after any sporting performance in my career, and physically it can't be compared with classic Trial. There, luckily, I do everything within 2 minutes and that's it. Thanks to the guys from the team, Aleš and my family for their help and support.”</em> said Vlasta, commenting on setting the record</p>\n\n<p>On the same day Martin Šimůnek and Michal Budský rode an exhibition at a witch-burning night, making a pleasant trip to Hořepník. The weather was kind to them and the turnout was good, so thanks for the invitation and hopefully again next year.</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/q3vES5izZfY?si=7sL56-GOtxwpZv1y\n</div></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2FIMG_9108.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2FIMG_9108.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-250774\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2FIMG_9105.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2FIMG_9105.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-250772\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2FIMG_9099.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2FIMG_9099.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-250770\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2FIMG_9080.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://fir